// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 16-aggregates
// facility: rule.agg.index-vec [Index-Vec] (`*v[k]` written reaches the element by index_exclusive, D-0219, CHG-0258); spec/08 [Read-Ref-Through-Shared]; conf.vec-of-exclusive-refs-write-element
// kind: positive
// expect: ok
//
// `*w[0] = 5` with `w : Vec<ref<i32, exclusive>>` writes through the
// stored reference. The place written is `*w[0]`, so `w[0]` is reached by
// `index_exclusive`: through the shared `index_shared`, the stored
// exclusive reference would be read as a shared one (D-0218) and the write
// rejected. Read in value position, `*w[0]` goes through `index_shared`
// and reads through that shared borrow.

import std;

fn main() : u8
{
    i32 x = 7;
    {
        Vec<ref<i32, exclusive>> w = Vec::new();
        Vec::push(&mut w, &mut x);
        *w[0] = 5;
        *w[0] = *w[0] + 1;
    }
    if (x != 6)
    {
        return 1;
    }
    0
}
